Keep sRGB encoding in 8-bit aux buffers (color shift of moved/transformed windows)

Problem: since the HDR work (#3023, 2026-06) every aux render target is linear,
but aux buffers are 8-bit unless the output is HDR. Linear values in 8 bits lose
most levels of dark colors, and the channels round differently: a window drawn
through a transformer (move/drag, scale, animations) changes its tint. Measured
in a nested Wayfire (Vulkan renderer, SDR): a dark grey window (24,25,28) shows
as (22,22,28) in the scale view. The GLES2 renderer ignores color transforms
and is not affected.
Fix: an aux buffer is linear only with a 16-bit format (the HDR case); an 8-bit
aux buffer keeps sRGB, as the comment in render_target_t already said.
Upstream: not reported yet.
Remove when: upstream picks the aux encoding by precision (or always allocates
16-bit). Check: nested Wayfire with WLR_RENDERER=vulkan, a dark grey window,
scale/toggle over IPC; the pixel value must not change.
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

diff --git a/src/render.cpp b/src/render.cpp
index 50b8316b..e5710148 100644
--- a/src/render.cpp
+++ b/src/render.cpp
@@ -218,13 +218,34 @@ std::shared_ptr<wf::texture_t> wf::texture_t::from_texture(wlr_texture *texture)
     return tex;
 }
 
+/**
+ * Linear values need more than 8 bits per channel: in an 8-bit buffer dark colors lose most of their
+ * levels, and the channels round differently (a visible color shift). 8-bit aux buffers keep sRGB.
+ */
+static wlr_color_transfer_function aux_transfer_function(wlr_buffer *buffer)
+{
+    wlr_dmabuf_attributes dmabuf;
+    if (buffer && wlr_buffer_get_dmabuf(buffer, &dmabuf))
+    {
+        switch (dmabuf.format)
+        {
+          case DRM_FORMAT_ABGR16161616F:
+          case DRM_FORMAT_XBGR16161616F:
+          case DRM_FORMAT_ABGR16161616:
+          case DRM_FORMAT_XBGR16161616:
+            return WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_EXT_LINEAR;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_SRGB;
+}
+
 std::shared_ptr<wf::texture_t> wf::texture_t::from_aux(auxilliary_buffer_t& buffer)
 {
     auto tex = from_buffer(buffer.get_buffer(), buffer.get_texture());
 
-    // We keep aux buffers in linear color space.
     auto transform = tex->get_color_transform();
-    transform.transfer_function = WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_EXT_LINEAR;
+    transform.transfer_function = aux_transfer_function(buffer.get_buffer());
     tex->set_color_transform(transform);
     return tex;
 }
@@ -589,11 +610,11 @@ wf::render_target_t::render_target_t(const render_buffer_t& buffer) : render_buf
 wf::render_target_t::render_target_t(const auxilliary_buffer_t& buffer) : render_buffer_t(
         buffer.get_buffer(), buffer.get_size())
 {
-    // By default, we keep aux buffers in SRGB color space, as SRGB is efficiently implemented in Vulkan.
     // set_color_transform() takes its own reference; drop the one init gave us.
-    auto linear = wlr_color_transform_init_linear_to_inverse_eotf(WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_EXT_LINEAR);
-    set_color_transform(linear, WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_EXT_LINEAR);
-    wlr_color_transform_unref(linear);
+    const auto tf = aux_transfer_function(buffer.get_buffer());
+    auto transform = wlr_color_transform_init_linear_to_inverse_eotf(tf);
+    set_color_transform(transform, tf);
+    wlr_color_transform_unref(transform);
 }
 
 void wf::render_target_t::copy_from(const render_target_t& other)
